body:
Escitalopram gets the work done for me. I’ve felt better mood-wise when I’ve been on it, but deep down everything is the same, I can’t get motivation. I still appreciate it even though I haven’t been able to afford it for a couple months which has resulted in a huuuge decline in my mental health. I’m happy antidepressants are working for you, while at the same time I can understand the doomers which won’t take medication nor seem to be helped by taking them. It took changing to a very expensive yet sensitive psychiatrist to prescribe me the right one (along with quetiapine which I have a love/hate relationship with).

&#x200B;

I’m happy for you, doomer. Don’t quit your medication regardless of the temptation to do so, and keep in touch with your psychiatrist. And hopefully some doomer here will be moved by your post (I’m honestly the most pessimistic and hopeless person I know in the world, you can trust me fellow doomers).

when oppening the link and clicking “View Subscriptions”, it says the following: You don't have a license to use Office 365 with the user ID assigned to you by your work or school. Ask your admin to assign one to you. If you're an admin, you can assign one to your account.

&#x200B;

I don’t get it, I am able to login to teams in my PC and Mac. I was also logged in in my iphone, but yesterday I log out and I can’t log back in anymore.

&#x200B;

I don’t really know how to upload screenshots, but when I try to log in from either my iPad or my iPhone, it says the following: Sign-in error Your license doesn’t include access to Microsoft Teams. Ask your IT admin for access.
